= The End of the Lib-Lab Pact

David Steel has confirmed that the Lib-Lab Pact ends with this session of Parliament. The Liberals got little from it except survival, and their poll ratings collapsed while it lasted.

From the autumn, Callaghan will govern as a minority, depending vote by vote on whoever he can persuade. [? if lib_relation >= 40 : Steel's people have made it known they are open to talking. ?]
